sections = sections.replace("Recorded feedback was paraphrased rather than quoted.", "The feedback comments are the teachers' own words. For example, Anurag wrote, ‘I like how the platform provides an integrated differentiation option that's a blessing for a beginner teacher like me... I need to plan 4 lessons everyday and I can do them now in 30 minutes...’ Janhavi wrote, ‘I would like to see if the AI can pull context of the story to desgin the assignment than keeping it general... maybe can add pictures given grade 4 children learn visuals.’ Anjali wrote, ‘I would like to make the assignment more rigorous and bring questions around real life.’ The spelling and punctuation are preserved from pilot.db.")
sections = sections.replace("The token figures below are recorded aggregates from the pilot database; monthly scenarios are assumptions rather than observed usage.", f"The demo trace recorded {trace_tokens:,} input tokens, {trace_cached:,} cached input tokens, and ${trace_cost:.6f} model cost across its full loop. The 5-sheet reader portion cost ${sum(float(x.get('cost_usd') or 0) for x in trace_calls if x.get('agent_name') == 'answer_sheet_reader'):.6f}, or ${sum(float(x.get('cost_usd') or 0) for x in trace_calls if x.get('agent_name') == 'answer_sheet_reader') / 5:.6f} per sheet. Caching covered {trace_cached / trace_tokens * 100:.1f}% of trace input tokens. With an assumption of 22 school days and two loops per day, multiply the measured loop cost by 44 for one teacher-month, then by 100 or 10,000 for scale scenarios; these are arithmetic scenarios, not observed usage. The token figures are recorded aggregates from the pilot database.")
